<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harju County</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Harjumaa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harju County is a county in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> that includes the capital, Tallinn. The historic land of Harjumaa, known in German as Harrien, was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1219, and its German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> formed the knighthood of Harrien, which in 1561 submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> together with Wierland. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-georges-night-uprising">St George's Night Uprising</a> of 1343 against German rule began there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harju-county.jpg" alt="Harju County" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayuntamiento,_vistas_panor%C3%A1micas_desde_Toompea,_Tallin,_Estonia,_2012-08-05,_DD_21.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
